-- title:
--   Two generators modulo kerπ from an adjoint duality
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $A$ a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, and $k$ a field that is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\mathcal{O}\to k$ surjective, and let $\pi\colon A\to k$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism. Let $P$ be an $A$-module and let $W$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space which also carries an $A$-module structure such that each $r\in\mathcal{O}$ acts on $W$ through $A$ exactly as it acts through $k$, i.e. $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{\mathcal{O},A}(r)\cdot w=\mathrm{algebraMap}_{\mathcal{O},k}(r)\cdot w$ for all $r,w$. Let $\beta\colon P\to \operatorname{Hom}_k(W,k)$ be a homomorphism of additive groups which is adjoint for the two $A$-actions, $\beta(a\cdot m)(w)=\beta(m)(a\cdot w)$ for all $a\in A$, $m\in P$, $w\in W$, whose left kernel lies in the $A$-span of $\{a\cdot n : \pi(a)=0,\ n\in P\}$ (if $\beta(m)=0$ then $m$ belongs to that span) and whose right kernel vanishes (if $\beta(m)(w)=0$ for all $m\in P$ then $w=0$). Assume finally that there are $u,v\in W$ such that every $w\in W$ annihilated by all $a\in A$ with $\pi(a)=0$ is of the form $c\cdot u+d\cdot v$ with $c,d\in k$. Then there exist $x,y\in P$ such that the $A$-submodule of $P$ generated by $\{x,y\}$ together with $\{a\cdot m : \pi(a)=0,\ m\in P\}$ is all of $P$.
--
--   This is the linear-algebra step, in the form used by Wiles, by which a duality between a module $P$ and a finite-dimensional space $W$ transfers a bound of two on the dimension of the $\ker\pi$-torsion of $W$ into the assertion that $P$ is generated by two elements modulo $\ker\pi\cdot P$. It is applied to the corner submodule of a first cohomology group attached to an absolutely irreducible representation.
